odes Policy 2026R0112D"},{"label":"Ohio pharmacist exception (closed list)","quote":"In addition, Ohio Medicaid allows Pharmacists to bill E/M CPT 99202, 99203, 99211, 99212, 99213, 99214, 99215, 90460, 90471, 90472, 90473, 90474 and 96372","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan — Nonphysician Health Care Professionals Billing E/M Codes Policy 2026R0112D"},{"label":"N.P./P.A. billing identity","quote":"Use their tax ID and NPI, and we will process the claims according to their agreement.","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan Ohio — 2026 Care Provider Manual (PMG 20251008-164146)"},{"label":"P.A.s may not enrol as solo providers","quote":"N.P.s may enroll with the state as solo care providers, but P.A.s cannot. P.A.s must be part of a group practice.","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan Ohio — 2026 Care Provider Manual (PMG 20251008-164146)"},{"label":"ODM screening, enrolment and credentialing prerequisite","quote":"Please note, you are not able to render services to Medicaid members until you are fully screened, enrolled and credentialed (if required) by Ohio Medicaid.","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan Ohio — 2026 Care Provider Manual (PMG 20251008-164146)"},{"label":"telehealth practitioner list — eligibility to deliver telehealth, not to report E/M","quote":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan recognizes the CMS-designated practitioners eligible to be reimbursed for Telehealth services: Examples of practitioners are listed below: Physician Nurse practitioner Physician assistant Nurse-midwife Clinical nurse specialist Registered dietitian or nutrition professional Clinical psychologist Clinical social worker Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetists","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan — Telehealth/Virtual Health Policy"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.92, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'c1a1d3f2-6b74-4b8e-9a21-7c5e2f4d8a02'::uuid, 'UnitedHealthcare Community Plan will not reimburse E/M services (CPT codes 98000-98016, 99091, 99202-99499) when r