  ('059f8858-1715-4964-84a3-d70f04b5fd36'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000302'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', 'G0181', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"No service may be rendered to, or billed for, an Ohio Medicaid member until the provider has been screened, enrolled and credentialed (where credentialing is required) by Ohio Medicaid — ODM, not the plan, credentials Medicaid managed care providers, and contracting with UnitedHealthcare is a separate step on top of it. N.P.s and P.A.s bill under their own tax ID and NPI per their collaborative agreement, and a P.A. may not enrol as a solo provider. IMPORTANT SCOPE LIMIT: UnitedHealthcare''s Nonphysician Health Care Professionals E/M policy (2026R0112D) defines E/M as CPT 98000-98016, 99091 and 99202-99499. This code sits outside those ranges, so that policy''s provider-type restriction does NOT govern it — do not assume the E/M billing prohibition applies here. TELEHEALTH — DO NOT CONFLATE THE TWO LISTS: UnitedHealthcare''s Telehealth/Virtual Health Policy names the CMS-designated practitioners eligible to be reimbursed for telehealth services, and that list does include registered dietitians, clinical psychologists and clinical social workers. It is a list of who may deliver a telehealth service, NOT a list of who may report an E/M code. A clinical social worker, dietitian or psychologist on that telehealth list still may not report this code; delivering the visit by audio-video changes the modifier, not the eligible biller.","appliesToService":"\"render services to Medicaid members\" — Ohio Medicaid screening, enrolment and credentialing prerequisite","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan Ohio — 2026 Care Provider Manual (PMG 20251008-164146)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"N.P./P.A. billing identity","quote":"Use their tax ID and NPI, and we will process the claims according to their agreement.","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan Ohio — 2026 Care Provider Manual (PMG 20251008-164146)"},{"label":"P.A.s may not enrol as solo providers","quote":"N.P.s may enroll with the state as solo care providers, but P.A.s cannot. P.A.s must be part of a group practice.","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan Ohio — 2026 Care Provider Manual (PMG 20251008-164146)"},{"label":"the E/M policy''s code ranges, which exclude this code","quote":"CPT guidance instructs that E/M (CPT codes 98000-98016, 99091, 99202-99499) should only be reported by Physicians or other qualified health care professionals. In accordance with CMS guidelines, the only qualified health care professionals that may report E/M services are nurse practitioners (NP), clinical nurse specialists (CNS), certified nurse midwives (CNM) and Physician assistants (PA), none of which are considered nonphysician health care professionals for purposes of this policy.","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan — Nonphysician Health Care Professionals Billing E/M Codes Policy 2026R0112D"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.60, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'c1a1d3f2-6b74-4b8e-9a21-7c5e2f4d8a01'::uuid, 'Please note, you are not able to render services to Medicaid members until you are fully screened, enrolled and credentialed (if required) by Ohio Medicaid.', 'extract:denial-rules-round2-2026-08'),
  ('2415e781-9f0b-4bb7-8c39-032e4391192e'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000302'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"Depends on network status. An OUT-OF-NETWORK physician, facility or other health care professional must obtain prior authorization for all procedures and services — there is no visit threshold and no carve-out other than emergency or urgent care, so this reaches every service a palliative practice bills. For an IN-NETWORK provider, this code appears on no prior-authorization code list in the 11/1/2025 requirements document, and the document states no service-specific prior authorization for it. Note the document''s \"Home health care\" row (G0151, G0152, G0153, G0156, G0299, G0300) is a home health agency benefit and does NOT govern physician home-visit E/M.","appliesToService":"Out-of-network physicians, facilities and other health care professionals — General Information section of the Ohio Medicaid prior authorization requirements effective 11/1/2025","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan of Ohio — Prior Authorization Requirements, effective 11/1/2025","supportingQuotes":[]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.85, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'c1a1d3f2-6b74-4b8e-9a21-7c5e2f4d8a03'::uuid, 'Prior authorization is not required for emergency or urgent care. Out-of-network physicians, facilities and other health care professionals must request prior authorization for all procedures and services', 'extract:denial-rules-round2-2026-08'),
  ('a407f893-5f61-4460-891a-118be2131556'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000302'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99342', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"Depends on network status. An OUT-OF-NETWORK physician, facility or other health care professional must obtain prior authorization for all procedures and services — there is no visit threshold and no carve-out other than emergency or urgent care, so this reaches every service a palliative practice bills. For an IN-NETWORK provider, this code appears on no prior-authorization code list in the 11/1/2025 requirements document, and the document states no service-specific prior authorization for it. Note the document''s \"Home health care\" row (G0151, G0152, G0153, G0156, G0299, G0300) is a home health agency benefit and does NOT govern physician home-visit E/M.","appliesToService":"Out-of-network physicians, facilities and other health care professionals — General Information section of the Ohio Medicaid prior authorization requirements effective 11/1/2025","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan of Ohio — Prior Authorization Requirements, effective 11/1/2025","supportingQuotes":[]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.85, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'c1a1d3f2-6b74-4b8e-9a21-7c5e2f4d8a03'::uuid, 'Prior authorization is not required for emergency or urgent care. Out-of-network physicians, facilities and other health care professionals must request prior authorization for all procedures and services', 'extract:denial-rules-round2-2026-08'),
