  ('a9f483d4-1412-44c0-8f80-6160d7920672'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000302'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"Every visit note must record appropriate vital signs (height, weight and BMI measured annually) plus chief complaint, physical assessment, diagnosis and treatment plan — the last four are marked as critical elements. Entries must be signed and dated and every page must carry the member name or identification number. Records are subject to UnitedHealthcare''s periodic quality medical record review, with a passing score of 85% or better expected, so a visit note missing these elements is exposed on audit. IF THE VISIT WAS DELIVERED BY TELEHEALTH: it must be documented to the same extent as an in-person visit, reflecting what occurred during the visit, and the note must additionally state that the visit was done through audio-video telecommunications. Telehealth lowers no documentation requirement — it adds one.","appliesToService":"\"Problem evaluation and management\" — the manual''s per-visit medical record charting standard, plus the telehealth documentation standard from the Telehealth/Virtual Health Policy","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan Ohio — 2026 Care Provider Manual (PMG 20251008-164146)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"telehealth documentation standard","quote":"A patient visit performed through Telehealth should be documented to the same extent as an in-person visit, reflecting what occurred during the visit. The healthcare professionals should also document that the visit was done through audio-video telecommunications.","document":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan — Telehealth/Virtual Health Policy"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.85, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'c1a1d3f2-6b74-4b8e-9a21-7c5e2f4d8a01'::uuid, 'Documentation for each visit includes: • Appropriate vital signs (measurement of height, weight and BMI annually) – Chief complaint* – Physical assessment* – Diagnosis* – Treatment plan*', 'extract:denial-rules-round2-2026-08'),
