  ('0df4787d-dea9-44b1-8548-a738a7045c42'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000302'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan applies a maximum daily frequency edit per procedure. The manual does NOT publish the numeric limit for this code — treat the number as unknown and confirm it with the plan. What the manual does state is the consequence: to exceed a procedure''s maximum daily frequency you must submit the medical records justifying medical necessity, otherwise the claim is subject to denial. This matters for same-day repeat visits and for a prolonged-service or care-management code billed alongside a visit.","appliesToService":"claim submission and reconsideration guidance — exceeding a procedure''s maximum daily frequency","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"UnitedHealthcare Community Plan Ohio — 2026 Care Provider Manual (PMG 20251008-164146)","supportingQuotes":[]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.60, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'c1a1d3f2-6b74-4b8e-9a21-7c5e2f4d8a01'::uuid, 'the maximum daily frequency for a procedure, submit the medical records justifying medical necessity', 'extract:denial-rules-round2-2026-08'),
